sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg activator-inhibitor at diffusion ratio r = 10, with the Turing onset wavenumber k_c and the maximum-growth wavelength k_sigma calibrated so the expressed scale is 2.117 µm (2.1 µm, log10 = -5.674) at 0 Ma. D_u sweep Pearson r = 0.989 against lambda(k_sigma), RMSE 0.41 px. Equal-diffusion ablation amplitude ratio is ~0. Detail-scale wavelengths are 1.958 µm (affinis), 2.117 µm (americana), 1.900 µm (ananassae), buffered by body-length exponent 0.35 relative to the 96/139/85 µm primordium siblings. Species-card CV similarity of the growth GIF is 79.0 (12 frames, 640×520). Orientation KS on 12 histogram bins is 0.5 and is not yet a pixel-sample test. Overall 83.5/100 (faithfulness 82.0, reproducibility 87.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 409578 B, 1248×984 px, artifact_sha256 2de831d22be834c643aa1e938701f9b96b1c232a8946b381d28e9d0805432bb1 (sha256 2de831d22be834c643aa1e938701f9b96b1c232a8946b381d28e9d0805432bb1), spec_fingerprint 2f4962a2f9aad429899235fd1af99851f464c94cb46349fdccbc4240f10a01bb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2f4962a2f9aad429899235fd1af99851f464c94cb46349fdccbc4240f10a01bb; artifact_sha256: 2de831d22be834c643aa1e938701f9b96b1c232a8946b381d28e9d0805432bb1; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_americana_specimen.jpg=c14927be1f313896..., datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=54ba0c292c786355..., datasets/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=1770ea1c999fdf81...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic and largely cis-regulatory, at body-color scale. | Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018: D. ananassae is in the sequenced Sophophora genomes; D. americana sits in the virilis radiation.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v with a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, integrated by a Fourier semi-implicit step. | Detail-scale wavelengths lambda_i = 2.117e-6 * (L_i / L_americana)^0.35 for affinis, americana, and ananassae. | Physical ruler that sets lambda(k_sigma) = 2.117 µm on the americana anchor.; transfer_boundary: The 2.117 µm figure is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified here with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not report that length. | Predecessor and successor are campaign chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not a fossil ancestor-descendant series.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the repository species card is a micrograph of the ocellus. It is a brown pigment card with a 100 µm scale bar. | Does not claim the X–4 fusion or red/brown puparium is a term in the reaction-diffusion equations. | Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044, which Crossref returns as 404.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: GIF caption uses λ and µm, which the default PIL font does not draw. Replace with ASCII.",
            "remediation needed: R2: Orientation KS is ks_2samp on 12 histogram bins (statistic 0.5). Recompute on pixel orientation samples and report that distance.",
            "remediation needed: R3: Add a near-onset run (r closer to r_c ≈ 8.57) showing the fractional gap (lambda_sigma - lambda_c) / lambda_c shrinks relative to r = 10.",
            "remediation needed: R4: Single species card and a single assessor. The card is not an ocellar micrograph; do not treat a higher score as anatomical validation." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.835"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; no second provider in this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai/> .
}

